  "limitations": [
    "Browser acceptance mocks the browser Push subscription and provider, then injects a test PushEvent into the actual service worker; no external provider delivery is claimed.",
    "WebKit iPhone emulation verifies installation guidance; physical iPhone/iPad installation and delivery remain unqualified.",
    "The default VAPID contact is development-only (.invalid); real sending requires an operator contact and Internet access to the browser provider.",
    "Workshop guardians and linked commits use explicitly identified PUBLIC_TEST_ONLY keys; the public pilot and voting cryptography retain their existing qualification limits.",
    "SQLite is experimental in the locked Node version. Abrupt process exit was tested on Windows; electrical power loss was not qualified.",
    "The discovery API cannot prove completeness. Pinned genesis and authenticated proofs prevent fabricated announcements; an indexer can omit an opening.",
    "An accepted provider request and the local delivery commit cannot be atomic. A crash at that boundary can repeat a delivery; the job and browser deduplication remain idempotent.",
    "Subscription data can reveal followed networks. It remains off-chain and separate from accounts and ballots.",
    "Public deployment, signed releases, emergency tooling, external audits and mass-load qualification remain in later milestones."
  ]
